 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "A type node is either a primitive string (\"int\", \"char\" or \"float\"), a generic string (\"T\" followed by one digit) or a tuple, written as a non-empty JSON list of type nodes (tuples nest, at most 20 levels). Formatting: a primitive or generic prints as itself; a tuple prints as \"[\" + its element strings joined by \", \" + \"]\"; a function type prints as \"(\" + the parameter strings joined by \", \" + \") -> \" + the return string. Level 2 (inferred): a function with parameter types params and return type returnType is called with argument types args (concrete nodes, no generics). Match each argument against its parameter: a primitive must equal the argument exactly, a tuple must meet a tuple of the same length element by element, and a generic binds to the whole argument node (which may be a tuple); every occurrence of the same generic must bind to an identical node. Return the formatted return type with every bound generic replaced by its binding (generics that are not bound stay as written), or null when the argument count differs or any argument does not match.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk14-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
